<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trinity Cathedral, Pskov</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Trinity Cathedral in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pskov">Pskov</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, is the city's main <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> church, standing inside the Krom citadel. Tradition places the first church on the site in the 10th century, and the present building dates from the 1680s and 1690s. In the Pskov Republic the cathedral held the state archives and treasury, and the veche assembly met beside it.</p></div>
